{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-85ddbd3709ffcaff4fc3","statement":"On $V_{l}\\ot V_{m}$, we have\n\n\\[\nb_i\\wb^{(\\lb,\\mb)}_{\\jb}\n=D'_1\\wb^{(\\lb-\\eb_s+\\eb_{s+1},\\mb)}_{\\jb-\\eb_s}\n+D'_2\\wb^{(\\lb,\\mb-\\eb_s+\\eb_{s+1})}_{\\jb-\\eb_s}\n+D'_3\\wb^{(\\lb+\\eb_s-\\eb_{s+1},\\mb)}_{\\jb-\\eb_{s+1}}\n+D'_4\\wb^{(\\lb,\\mb+\\eb_s-\\eb_{s+1})}_{\\jb-\\eb_{s+1}},\n\\]\n\nwhere\n\n\\begin{align*}\nD'_1&=-q^{-j_s-j_{s+1}+l_s+m_{s+1}+1}[j_s],\\quad\nD'_2=[j_s],\\\\\nD'_3&=-q^{-j_s-j_{s+1}+l_{s+1}+m_{s+1}+1}[j_{s+1}],\\quad\nD'_4=q^{-2j_s-2j_{s+1}+l_s+l_{s+1}+2m_{s+1}+2}[j_{s+1}].\n\\end{align*}","source_id":"arXiv:2012.00967","cluster":"mathematics","statement_sha256":"6f2a41ab27b8ca349566ff3fce91c84a1711f05a4cd8a2225f4da9a3fab21af2","kind":"proposition","label":"Proposition 8","ref_key":"prop:bw","name":"","order":13,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.00967","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"d1adc339d796c1ac2f8b9eb47b789e0355426463b407ef73101192b096da360b","line":524,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-26T14:00:38+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":478,"math_hints":75}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:2012.00967","title":"Solution to the reflection equation related to the $\\iota$quantum group of type AII","abstract":"A solution to the reflection equation associated to a coideal subalgebra of $U_q(A_{2n-1}^{(1)})$ of type AII in the symmetric tensor representations is presented. If parameters of the coideal subalgebra are suitably chosen, the $K$ matrix does not depend on the quantum parameter $q$ and still agrees with a solution in arXiv:nlin/0411044 at $q=0$.","authors":["Hiroto Kusano","Masato Okado"],"year":"2020","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.00967","cluster":"mathematics","macros":{"Q":"{\\mathbb Q}","Z":"{\\mathbb Z}","eb":"\\boldsymbol{e}","jb"